The Members module allows you to invite users to your workspace and assign roles, teams, and responsibilities.

## Members Page

Collaborate seamlessly by managing all users in one centralized system.

## Members Table

{% table %}
- Member Name
- Teams
- Email
- Team Role
- Actions
{% /table %}

## Add Team Member

### Purpose

Invite a new user into your workspace and define their role and access.

## Member Form Fields

### First Name *

Enter the first name.

**Example:** John

### Last Name *

Enter the last name.

**Example:** Doe

### Role *

Select user role.

**Example:**

- Member
- Manager
- Client
- Admin

### Position

Define job title or role.

**Example:**

- Designer
- Developer
- Project Manager

### Email *

Enter valid email address.

**Example:** john@example.com

### Select Teams

Assign user to one or more teams.

### Send Invitation Now

A toggle, on by default, shown only when adding a new member (not when editing an existing one).

- **On:** the invitation email goes out immediately.
- **Off:** the member is created without emailing an invite — send it later from the Members table.

## Invitation Status

A member who hasn't accepted their invitation yet shows a badge next to their name:

- **Not Invited** — created with **Send Invitation Now** off; no invite email has gone out yet.
- **Invitation Pending** — an invite email was sent and is awaiting acceptance.
- **Invitation Expired** — the invite link expired before it was accepted.

A member who has accepted shows no badge.

## Managing a Pending Invitation

For any member who is **Not Invited**, **Invitation Pending**, or **Invitation Expired**, open the row's **⋯** actions menu (Admin and Manager only) to:

- **Send Invitation** — sends the invite email (or resends it). This can be temporarily disabled shortly after the last send, to prevent sending duplicates in quick succession.
- **Copy Invitation URL** — copies the same acceptance link the invitation email contains, so you can share it yourself instead of resending the email.

## Member Details Page

